WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:06.319
OK, I want to deal now with something that
many of you and I have been noticing about

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:08.410
coronavirus lately.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.410
Cases have exploded.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:17.050
I mean, just insane numbers of cases and it's
specifically in some states and not in others.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.780
But the death numbers have not been high for
now.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:21.780
That's a good thing.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.550
I don't want anybody catching coronavirus.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.510
I don't want anybody dying from Corona virus.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:32.840
But the question is, based on the case numbers,
we would expect deaths to be higher in some

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.690
of these states, especially ones where we're
learning that the I.C.E. user maxed out.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.240
So what's going on there now is a reminder.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.330
I have no political perspective here.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.120
My my ideology on the virus is health.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.920
It just so happens the president we have has
failed miserably on corona virus.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.110
But I want to find the real explanation and
I want to find the truth.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:01:02.059
So here's a few ideas that have been proposed
about why there have been so many cases, but

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:05.920
relatively fewer deaths than we were seeing
a few months ago.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:06.920
OK.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:12.429
One possibility that's been proposed is that
we are getting better at treating Corona virus.

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:18.689
In other words, if you get sick enough to
go into the hospital, doctors are now better

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:23.280
at treating because we have three months of
experience and thus you would expect the death

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.280
rate to be lower.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:28.939
In fact, there is a study called Decreased
in Hospital Mortality in patients with Koven

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:30.189
19 pneumonia.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:34.259
And it says that in a lot of countries, fewer
people are going to the hospital and dying.

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:39.289
And it's a combination of some hospitals being
less overrun with a better understanding of

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:41.430
how patients should be treated.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:42.430
Reminder.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:43.430
That's why we locked down.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.069
When you locked down, you keep the hospitals
less full.

00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:51.819
So the sick people get better care and you
allow time for doctors to learn to properly

00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:52.819
treat the disease.

00:01:52.819 --> 00:01:57.020
So hopefully, by the time you get it or your
loved one gets it, the medical system is better

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.509
equipped to treat.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:01:59.509
Very good.

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:00.509
That's one possibility.

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:06.350
Second possibility for why there are a ton
of cases and not as many deaths is that we

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.560
just haven't seen the deaths yet.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:15.579
OK, the idea in general is it's like twenty
two days from test to death.

00:02:15.579 --> 00:02:17.600
You get a positive test.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.000
It's often five days before you end up in
the hospital.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.620
It's often 17 days from hospitalization to
death.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:29.709
So it's like a 22 day delay between cases
and deaths.

00:02:29.709 --> 00:02:33.829
The current spike started, I call it June
16th.

00:02:33.829 --> 00:02:38.879
If this is the explanation that we've just
haven't seen the deaths yet, we would expect

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:42.290
deaths to spike around June 7th or 8th.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.940
I hope it doesn't happen if it is that that's
what's going on.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.680
The death numbers are going to get very, very
ugly very, very soon.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:56.760
Third possibility for why we have so many
cases and relatively few deaths is that older

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.909
folks are better protecting themselves and
staying home.

00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:05.129
And it's the younger people that are testing
positive younger people, much more likely

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.910
not to need hospitalization, much less likely
to die.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.250
That would be a possibility.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.900
We don't have the full data on that.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.590
That's really an empirical question.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.730
We just don't have the full data on that.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:17.730
So we would have to see.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:22.230
I know that there are some cities that are
saying we are seeing more young people get

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.719
it, fewer older folks get it.

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:27.920
We need to see that at the state level, at
the federal level.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:36.349
Lastly, there are some doctors arguing that
the virus is mutating to be less serious,

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:41.879
that at this point the virus has weakened
and thus those who are infected.

00:03:41.879 --> 00:03:46.019
Are getting a less serious version of it than
what was going around in March, April and

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:47.170
early May.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:51.749
I don't want to say too much about that because
we don't know that to be the case.

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:53.049
It's a hypothesis.

00:03:53.049 --> 00:03:55.659
It presumably could be tested empirically.

00:03:55.659 --> 00:03:56.950
That's not been done.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:00.640
Most doctors are saying there is not actually
evidence of that right now.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:05.459
And so I don't want to risk giving people
the wrong idea with something that has not

00:04:05.459 --> 00:04:07.250
been demonstrated to be true.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:12.639
Still a lot to learn, but those are four of
the possibilities for why so far we are seeing

00:04:12.639 --> 00:04:18.070
unconscionable spikes in the number of cases,
but not yet, not yet seen.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:21.020
And hopefully we won't see corresponding numbers
of deaths.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.530
Let me know what you think about this.

